================================================================================
 Atomic Red Team — quick reference (art-1)
================================================================================
 Target Windows host : {{ atomic_target_host }}   (user: {{ atomic_target_user | default('vagrant') }})
 SSH private key      : ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
 Atomics folder       : ~/AtomicRedTeam/atomics
 Runner              : invoke-atomicredteam (pwsh module, already installed)

 The scenario already ran a first batch automatically. Below is how to run more
 tests by hand after logging into this VM.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1) Start pwsh and open ONE reusable session to the Windows target.
#    NOTE: the IP below is from when this VM was provisioned; if win-user-1 was
#    redeployed it changes — confirm with `lab deploy show <deployment>`.
pwsh
Import-Module invoke-atomicredteam -Force
$sess = New-PSSession -HostName {{ atomic_target_host }} -UserName {{ atomic_target_user | default('vagrant') }} -KeyFilePath $HOME/.ssh/id_ed25519 -SSHTransport -Options @{ StrictHostKeyChecking = "accept-new" }

# 2) Inspect a technique before running it:
Invoke-AtomicTest T1082 -ShowDetailsBrief
Invoke-AtomicTest T1082 -ShowDetails

# 3) Prereqs (many tests need tools/files first):
Invoke-AtomicTest T1059.001 -Session $sess -CheckPrereqs
Invoke-AtomicTest T1059.001 -Session $sess -GetPrereqs

# 4) Run specific test number(s):
Invoke-AtomicTest T1059.001 -TestNumbers 1 -Session $sess -PathToAtomicsFolder $HOME/AtomicRedTeam/atomics

# 5) Clean up afterwards (skip for tests whose artifact you want to keep):
Invoke-AtomicTest T1059.001 -TestNumbers 1 -Session $sess -Cleanup

# Run EVERY test for a technique (prereqs -> run -> cleanup):
Invoke-AtomicTest T1003 -Session $sess -GetPrereqs
Invoke-AtomicTest T1003 -Session $sess
Invoke-AtomicTest T1003 -Session $sess -Cleanup

# When finished:
Remove-PSSession $sess

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Notes
 - Tests execute ON the Windows target, so detections show up in Kibana from
   win-user-1 (Sysmon / Security 4688 / PowerShell 4104), not from this VM.
 - Traffic to the target goes over the management network by default, so you can
   filter it out of SIEM searches by source host if needed.
 - Full technique list: https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/tree/master/atomics
================================================================================
